ure below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M D   Electronically signed on  10 19  REMOVED_CASE_ID   SURGICAL ADDENDUM  10 20 06    Immunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the  following results for INVASIVE carcinoma  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Estrogen receptor POSITIVE  Progesterone receptor POSITIVE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NEGATIVE  1    Interpretation   Hormone receptor analysis  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the  carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows   positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  positive   low  0  to  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  negative 0  nuclei immunoreactive  The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet  been determined    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu analysis   Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor  cells   Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but only  a portion of the membrane is positive   Positive  2    Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in  10   of tumor cells   Positive  3    Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells   Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result   Some of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational  use only   Addendum  1 by Deborah A Dillon M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE   report_end  , Absent.
